{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\ns=open('recovery_explore_test.go').read().replace('TestAssuranceRecoverDecisionExploration','TestAssuranceRecoveryDecisionPreservation')\ns=s.replace('\\\"event\\\":\\\"first_decision\\\",\\\"origin\\\":1,\\\"instance\\\":0','\\\"event\\\":\\\"first_decision\\\",\\\"scenario\\\":\\\"one_crash_missing_slot\\\",\\\"origin\\\":target.id.replica,\\\"instance\\\":target.id.instance')\ns=s.replace('\\\"event\\\":\\\"second_decision\\\",\\\"origin\\\":1,\\\"instance\\\":0','\\\"event\\\":\\\"second_decision\\\",\\\"scenario\\\":\\\"one_crash_missing_slot\\\",\\\"origin\\\":second.id.replica,\\\"instance\\\":second.id.instance')\ns=s.replace(' // while dispatching the next PreAccept, as the run-loop select permits.',' // while dispatching the next PreAccept. Production has independent\\\\n // enqueue goroutines per decoded RPC and separate handler channels: the\\\\n // Commit enqueue/dispatch may remain pending during this finite suffix.')\ns=s.replace(' recoverer.startRecoveryForInstance(1,0)',' assuranceReportEvent(t,map[string]any{\\\"event\\\":\\\"missing_slot\\\",\\\"scenario\\\":\\\"one_crash_missing_slot\\\",\\\"origin\\\":later.Replica,\\\"instance\\\":0,\\\"known_high\\\":recoverer.crtInstance[1],\\\"slot_absent\\\":recoverer.InstanceSpace[1][0]==nil,\\\"failed_peer\\\":0,\\\"pending_commit_origin\\\":pendingCommit.Replica,\\\"pending_commit_instance\\\":pendingCommit.Instance})\\\\n recoverer.startRecoveryForInstance(1,0)')\ns=s.replace('if \"'!ok {t.Fatal(\"expected PrepareReply\")}; recoverer.handlePrepareReply(msg)'\"','if \"'!ok {t.Fatal(\"expected PrepareReply\")}; assuranceReportEvent(t,map[string]any{\"event\":\"recovery_support\",\"acceptor\":msg.AcceptorId,\"origin\":msg.Replica,\"instance\":msg.Instance,\"ballot\":msg.Ballot,\"vballot\":msg.VBallot,\"phase\":msg.Status}); recoverer.handlePrepareReply(msg)'\"')\nopen('recovery_safety_test.go','w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > build_safety_submission.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B_accept':b['unknowns']=[]\n if b['id']=='B_recover_select':\n  b['produces_fact_ids'].append('F_decision')\n  b['unknowns']=['Decision preservation under the combined self-report retagging, decoded report metadata and pending Commit schedule remains to be formally checked.']\nm['core_overview']['open_details'][1]='Eligible Accept retains its old local phase even when its replies support origin commitment. Decision preservation under subsequent recovery, self-report retagging and pending Commit remains open.'\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='Replica.handleAccept':s['reason']='Eligible Accept stores value metadata but retains its prior phase, which Prepare reports. The accepted-support local check is retained in Candidate/check records; wider decision preservation is a separate question.'\njson.dump(m,open('map-safety.json','w'),indent=2)\nchanges={k:dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S_accept','S_prepare','S_recover_select'],rationale='Replace the answered local phase-reporting unknown with the sourced retained-phase relationship; execution and interpretation remain in feedback.',preserves='The earlier C_accepted_phase_report and C_prepare_vballot_preserved requirements, dependencies and observations are unchanged. This update neither weakens those duties nor turns their local findings into safety evidence.') for k in ['B_accept','core_overview','surface:Replica.handleAccept']}\nchanges['B_recover_select']=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['S_recover_select'],rationale='The read committed recovery case installs selected status and metadata into the local instance. Record that additional producer of existing F_decision explicitly for the new decision-preservation question.',preserves='Existing local transport and phase-reporting checks retain their exact producer/consumer sources, premises, scope and observations. Adding the recovery decision producer does not change their duties or claim a different principal Fact meaning.')\nclaim='C_recovery_decision_preservation';bids=['BD_decision_commit','BD_decision_recovery','BD_decision_context','BD_decision_consume']\nss=['S_pa_reply','S_accept','S_commit','S_recover_start','S_recover_select','S_exec','S_run','S_readme_protocols']\ng=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=['S_accept','S_commit','S_recover_start','S_recover_select','S_exec','S_run','S_readme_protocols'],binding_ids=bids,derivation='The captured system declares replicated state-machine protocols and the executable configures tolerance of F crash failures. EPaxos coordinates a command batch by origin/instance identity. Its commit paths mark that identity decided, and execution consumes its commands. handleCommit refuses to replace already committed instances; recovery skips local committed entries with commands and prioritizes committed/accepted evidence before proposing anew. These interfaces and guards establish decision preservation as an applicable responsibility: a later recovery must not decide a different command batch for an already decided identity. This safety duty is not derived from whether the experiment differs or from assuming that the implemented recovery/quorum formulas satisfy it.',applicability='Static five-member thrifty crash-stop configuration, F=2, one actual stopped participant after initial quorum commitment, finite asynchronous delay of intact messages and legal instance recovery. Distinct nonfailed replicas observe commitment of the same origin/instance.',unresolved=['Specific causal contribution of each local defect is not isolated.','No completed client/application divergence is asserted.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Delayed Commit could teach the original decision if dispatched earlier, but safety must hold for permitted finite delayed dispatch.','Retained attributes and preaccepted recovery alternatives may protect other histories; the selected history exercises the actual combined recovery path.'])\nq=dict(question='Can missing-slot recovery at a nonfailed replica commit a command batch different from a prior commitment for the same origin/instance after one accepting peer crashes, while the original Commit remains legally pending?',importance='Two committed batches for one consensus identity violate decision agreement and can compromise replicated-state-machine correctness. This requires its own executed safety witness, not extrapolation from the local codec or phase defects.',source_ids=[],participants=['Original coordinator 1','Initial accepting peers 0 and 2','Recovery coordinator 3','Additional recovery peer 4'],objects=['Instance command batch at origin-row/slot identity','LeaderBookkeeping recovery selection','Pending Commit and later PreAccept messages'],contexts=['N=5,F=2,Thrifty=true,Durable=false','Peer 0 stops after initial acceptance; nodes 1/2/3/4 continue','Commit decoded before later PreAccept on a link, but independently enqueued/dispatched afterward'],event_paths=['Real conflicting proposals -> slow-path commitment 1.0 -> peer 0 crash -> later-slot PreAccept establishes known hole at replica 3 -> actual recovery Prepare replies -> actual new formation -> second commitment for 1.0'],activity_classes=['A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B_form','B_commit','B_authority','B_recover_select'],fact_ids=['F_decision'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_phase1':'Establishes legal client proposals and recovery phase-one values.','B_prepare_wire':'Carries actual remote support without patching the known codec omission.','B_accept':'Produces actual acceptor updates and acknowledgments.','B_membership':'Static participant and quorum parameter context.','B_recovery_watch':